<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements applied when the macOS bundle is codesigned. Hardened runtime
  is on (the Tauri bundler defaults `macOS.hardenedRuntime` to true) and is a
  hard requirement for notarization, so anything the app does that hardened
  runtime otherwise blocks has to be declared here.

  Keep this list minimal — every entry widens the hole hardened runtime is
  there to close.

  allow-jit: the wasmtime plugin host compiles plugin modules with Cranelift
  and maps the result executable. Under hardened runtime that needs MAP_JIT,
  which is gated on this entitlement. Without it, loading any WASM plugin
  (Web Radio ships in the bundle) crashes the process.

  Deliberately NOT present: `allow-unsigned-executable-memory` and
  `disable-library-validation`. Wasmtime uses MAP_JIT properly, so the
  narrower entitlement is enough; the app loads no third-party dylibs.
  App Sandbox entitlements (`com.apple.security.files.*`,
  `com.apple.security.network.*`) are irrelevant here — this is a
  Developer-ID-distributed app, not a Mac App Store one, so it is not
  sandboxed. Folder access is governed by TCC, driven by the purpose strings
  in Info.plist.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
